    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A number is called a mirror number if:<br><br>Reversing its digits produces a number different from the original.<br>The sum of the original number and its reversed number is a palindrome.<br>For example, 56 is a Mirror Number (56 != 65 and 56+65=121 is a palindrome.)<br><br>Your task is to determine whether a given number N is a mirror number.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">A positive integer N</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">&quot;Yes, N is a Mirror Number&quot; if N is a mirror number;<br>&quot;No, N is a Palindrome&quot; if N is a palindrome;<br>&quot;C&quot; otherwise, where M is the sum of N and its reversed number.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">56</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">Yes, 56 is a Mirror Number</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
